<title>SOUTH KOREA: Singdongbang reported for unfair trade.</title>
<headline>Singdongbang reported for unfair trade.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board (SSB) said on Monday it reported to prosecution office unfair trading by Shindongbang while the edible oil maker was seeking to take over Midopa Department Store.</p>
<p>The board said it has found some discrepancies in statements Shindongbang issued to clarify its position on the takeover.</p>
<p>In January the company circulated a statement saying rumours on its takeover bid for Midopa were groundless. But the company bought some shares of Midopa before issuing another statement in March that it was considering buying Midopa shares in the open market, the board said.</p>
</text>
